  "text": "2002A02 Draw a\nlabelled diagramme of cardiac muscle action potential\nhighlighting the sequence of changes in ionic conductances.\nExplain the terms “threshold”, “excitability”, “irritability” with the aid of a\ndiagramme.\nList:\n·\nIntro\n·\nGraph and conductances\n·\nDefinitions\nIntro:\nAction potential\n·\nAllows rapid, co-ordinated signalling\n·\nRapid depolarisation followed by repolarization\n·\nIon channels cycle through resting -> activated ->\n  inactivated states\nDeterminants of ion flux\n·\nChannel permeability: voltage dependent\n·\nElectrochemical gradients\no\nNa\n+\nand Ca\n2+\ninto cell, K\n+\nout of cell\no\nMainly\n  due to Na\n+\nK\n+\nATPase\nGraph and\nconductances:\nDefinitions:\nThreshold\n·\nMembrane potential at which a self-propagating\n  action potential is triggered\nExcitability\n·\n% of Na\n+\nchannels returned from inactivated to resting\n  state\n·\n∝\nrate of rise phase 0\nIrritability\n·\nCloseness to threshold\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
